note omegallm epool.om (aien-train#52, CONTRACT-V3 section 2): the bank-B pools of the x86efi target,
note one element each. The firmware image keeps the v2 bank-A capacity: ogeom refuses any shape whose
note parameters, BLK or activations pass bank A (lpool.om holds the Linux pools).
const OWWN ulong 1
global oww f64 1
const OGBN ulong 1
global ogb f64 1
const OABN ulong 1
global oab f64 1
